- op: discuss  # 337f
  at: '2026-10-12T10:58:42Z'  # 337f
  by: agent  # 337f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 337f
  clock: 3  # 337f
  nonce: 337f  # 337f
  message: "Fixed in PR #1550 (b89cc2e5a2). Root cause: generated-output directories (dist/build/_build/out/target/site/_site and the coverage-report names) were bare DEFAULT_EXCLUDES names matched as a path segment at any depth, so any same-named SOURCE directory was pruned silently (the same category error as Hugo's public/, removed in v0.5.1). Fix (owner direction: fix the condition, not the symptom): those names left DEFAULT_EXCLUDES; discovery.BUILD_OUTPUT_RULES now claims a directory only on its producing tool's evidence -- manifest beside it (Cargo.toml/pom.xml/build.sbt->target, mix.exs/rebar.config/conf.py->_build, mkdocs.yml+site_dir->site, Jekyll _config.yml->_site, Gradle->build, ...), declared output (package.json entry points, tsconfig outDir, action.yml runs.main), or a marker the tool writes into it (CMakeCache.txt, CACHEDIR.TAG, coverage report files, self-ignoring .gitignore); committed output is still output; untracked-in-git is only supporting evidence for dist/build/out beside a bare package.json. A name with no evidence is analysed. Pruned output is disclosed (stderr, sketch, supply_chain_summary.generated_output_skipped). supply_chain tier 4, the derived_skipped scan, ddg_build's walk and sketch's config filter ask the same rules. ADR-0004 point 7 amended. Corpus (273 repos): 354 dirs pruned before, 25 after; 329 (5,224 files, 2,796 source) now analysed. Evidence: find ~/whole_bunch_of_repos/plausible -path '*/site/*' (-name '*.ex' -o -name '*.exs') -> 28 files; find_elixir_files(plausible) restricted to */site/ -> 28 (was 0), toggle_live.ex and people.ex present -> True True. hypergumbo survey zoxide -> stderr 'Generated output not analysed: target/ (Cargo build). Recognised by the tool that writes each (ADR-0004).' Production-path test: test_generated_output.py::TestSourceDirectoriesWithOutputNames::test_plausible_site_modules_are_analysed and TestDisclosure::test_survey_prints_and_records_it."  # 337f
